> 
> For example, if you have an image file:
> 
> ```python
> with open("input.png", "rb") as f:
>     input_bytes = f.read()
> 
> output_bytes = img2img(
>     input_bytes,
>     "a watercolor painting of this scene, vibrant colors",
>     denoising_strength=0.5,
> )
> 
> with open("output.png", "wb") as f:
>     f.write(output_bytes)
> ```
> 
> `denoising_strength` is the key new parameter: around `0.2–0.4` preserves composition closely; `0.5–0.7` permits substantial restyling; values near `1.0` mostly regenerate the image.
